# DB DNS/NSS hard wall and one total address-attempt deadline.
register_gate "tests/test_db_dns_deadline.py" "DB DNS DEADLINE GATE: PASS" "database DNS hard deadline" "a fake wedged libc/NSS resolver returns the caller by its absolute deadline through the fixed daemon pool and bounded pending queue; URL and keyword DSNs retain the original hostname for TLS/SNI/certificate/pgpass semantics while each numeric hostaddr is attempted separately; every address attempt shares one total deadline; IP, Unix socket, hostless, and explicit-hostaddr DSNs bypass DNS; driver errors and test output never expose DSN secrets; DeliveryStore, live event connections, and server_dbops all route through the shared bounded connection leaf" "a DNS/NSS stall or multi-address database endpoint cannot monopolize the webhook worker or multiply connect timeout across addresses"
